  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 233 AM MDT WED SEP 23 2026\nTemperatures will cool to 5-15 degrees below normal area-wide \ncome Saturday. A trough digging off the west coast will pass-\nover the area late Sunday/early Sunday along with an associated \ncold front. While this trough and front will be weaker than that\nof Friday, it will help keep cooler conditions and breezy \nwest/northwest winds in place into the start of the next week. \nMoisture availability is in question for this next system. With \nan active eastern Pacific, tropical moisture could work it's way\nback up to support precipitation chances. However, return flow \nwill be limited with the quick one-two punch of these systems. \nRight now, am leaning towards another dry frontal passage with \nmoisture remaining south and east of our area. Long-range \nguidance doesn't handle the energy transfer with tropical \nsystems the best, but things should become more clear in the \ndays to come.",
